As discussed, this is regarding the move to the Liquibase Enterprise version.

We are currently using Liquibase Community version 5.0.1 in our pipeline. MTB is rolling out standardized Liquibase templates along with Enterprise support for teams that require Liquibase-based schema deployments. Since we already have a working Community-based implementation, there is currently a gap between our setup and the MTB standard pipeline.

Our existing pipeline includes a few additional capabilities tailored to our needs:

* SQL syntax check – runs before deployment to catch syntax issues in SQL files
* Liquibase reporting – currently handled using dbdocs for deployment visibility
* SQL unit testing (planned) – will be added soon using a Python framework with SQL-based test logic

Given these customizations, we are not planning to adopt the DBE team’s Liquibase template as-is. Our pipeline is designed based on our requirements and would need alignment rather than replacement.

For moving to the Enterprise version, we will need to:

* Update to the appropriate Docker image provided by the DBE team
* Leverage Liquibase office hours for any required guidance/support
* Align on version compatibility — the DBE team is expected to release their image on version 4.33, so we may either need to wait for a 5.0.1-compatible image or consider downgrading

